Third-party material
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Kwery is an independent implementation for Kotlin and Android. It is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or derived from the TanStack Query source code.
Where Kwery's behaviour matches TanStack Query, that is deliberate API parity,
documented in docs/roadmap/.

    TanStack Query
    https://github.com/TanStack/query
    Copyright (c) 2021-present Tanner Linsley
    Licensed under the MIT License

TanStack Query's documentation and its query-core test suite are used as the
reference for that parity work. **They are not redistributed in this
repository** — no TanStack Query material is committed here, and none is present
in any published Kwery artifact. Contributors fetch it locally at a pinned
revision with `./scripts/vendor-reference.sh`, into a gitignored `.reference/`
directory.

Some of Kwery's tests are ported from TanStack Query's test suite: re-expressed
in Kotlin against Kwery's own API, but with the test intent, and in places the
naming, following the originals. The MIT licence above covers that provenance.
Such tests cite the originating file in a comment.
